cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cancer literature + mechanism corpus — open index"
message: "If you use this index, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Garrison Node Project"
abstract: >
  An open, index-and-links corpus of 6,358 conventional and complementary cancer
  studies, each identifier-verified, classified by evidence type, and tagged by
  biological mechanism (12 nodes), with abstracts where openly available and a link
  to each source. Includes the public-domain USDA Duke Phytochemical & Ethnobotanical
  Database as the complementary-track mechanism substrate. Hypothesis-generating; not
  medical advice.
keywords:
  - pharmacovigilance
  - cancer
  - mechanism of action
  - ethnobotany
  - open data
license: CC0-1.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
